From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:37:41 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] sgx-pad

The SuperGrafx section gains a Pad row: 2 Buttons (the default) or 6
Buttons, kept in Config/sgx.txt as pad = 2 or 6 and answered as
sgx_default_joypad_type_p1 when the next card starts, as the core reads
it at load. With 6 buttons, Beetle SuperGrafx's Avenue Pad 6 takes III
and IV from RetroPad Y and X and V and VI from L and R: X and Y reach
the core raw (slot's turbo is passed by), L1 and R1 go to the game, and
the picture toggle moves to SELECT+X, as on the SNES. The mode is
latched when the card seats, the Virtual Boy Right Pad way, so a GBA
game after a six-button SuperGrafx game gets the GBA input and picture.
With 2 buttons nothing changes: X and Y are turbo, L1 and R1 are slot's.
